      "readme_path": "README.md",
      "readme_sha": "321a8b796bec72f5d7001a30521f4a6d1816a94b",
      "readme_excerpt": "Define and maintain complex project configuration through code. *projen* synthesizes project configuration files such as `package.json`, `tsconfig.json`, `.gitignore`, GitHub Workflows, eslint, jest, etc. from a well-typed definition written in JavaScript. As opposed to existing templating/scaffolding tools, *projen* is not a one-off generator. Synthesized files should never be manually edited (in fact, projen enforces that). To modify your project setup, users interact with rich strongly-typed class and execute `projen` to update their project configuration files. By defining a custom project type and using projen in multiple repositories, it's possible to update configuration files and CI/CD workflows across dozens (or hundreds!?) of",
